**Corollary 26.3 (same-history realization of the conditional inverse).** The degree-three moments can be acquired from zero without a raw-event archive: on an actual beta, using the old acquired count difference $h=A_{\rm old}-B_{\rm old}$, increment $\mathsf D$ by $2h-1$ and $\mathsf E$ by $3h^2-3h+1$; on alpha hold them. Include all retry, accepting-seed, return and completing letters, finish the writes before the same third latch, and hold that bank thereafter. Together with Hypothesis 7.1's actual $U$ and finite fields, these moments suffice for (SC.66)–(SC.68) and the same raw/record/relational inverse. This is a conditional acquired interface, not a new bound for the original length-only threshold $r_\mu(L)$.

Proof. Induction on the actual letters proves (SC.63) using only original fields and the returned letter. The selected-past holding and delivery contract is Hypothesis 18.1's same-history contract. For an acquired length $N$, $|\mathsf D|\le N(2N+1)$ and $0\le\mathsf E\le N(3N^2+3N+1)$, so their exact integer representations use $O(\log(N+2))$ data bits. The retry word still uses its separately paid $|U|$ bits and metadata. Arithmetic, original state/counts, installation, work, transmission, receiver storage and materialized output remain additional resource coordinates. Theorem 26.2 and Theorem 7.4 give the inverse. No separated prefix bank is assumed, and these moment costs are not a total-resource minimum. $\square$

